                    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                    "body": "My (initial) concern was that using the same full-height line separator for Progress and Indexing would make it easy to mix them up with the clock. Opting for a shorter separator makes it easier to distinguish the clock as one group and the LSP Progress/Indexing as a second group\r\n\r\nLet me know what you think would suit as a shorter form! I don't personally have a knack for designing in general, so suggestions here are always welcome!",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">My (initial) concern was that using the same full-height line separator for Progress and Indexing would make it easy to mix them up with the clock. Opting for a shorter separator makes it easier to distinguish the clock as one group and the LSP Progress/Indexing as a second group</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Let me know what you think would suit as a shorter form! I don't personally have a knack for designing in general, so suggestions here are always welcome!</p>",
                    "bodyText": "My (initial) concern was that using the same full-height line separator for Progress and Indexing would make it easy to mix them up with the clock. Opting for a shorter separator makes it easier to distinguish the clock as one group and the LSP Progress/Indexing as a second group\nLet me know what you think would suit as a shorter form! I don't personally have a knack for designing in general, so suggestions here are always welcome!",
