                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> My (initial) concern was that using the same full-height line separator for Progress and Indexing would make it easy to mix them up with the clock.\r\n\r\nFair point. Whichever design works for you.\r\n\r\n> Let me know what you think would suit as a shorter form! I don't personally have a knack for designing in general, so suggestions here are always welcome!\r\n\r\nI'd personally remove either \"Progress\" or \"Indexing\" altogether. Probably the former one. I suspect that they indeed describe different actions, but for me having the \"Indexing\" with its own progress report would be enough.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My (initial) concern was that using the same full-height line separator for Progress and Indexing would make it easy to mix them up with the clock.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fair point. Whichever design works for you.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Let me know what you think would suit as a shorter form! I don't personally have a knack for designing in general, so suggestions here are always welcome!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd personally remove either \"Progress\" or \"Indexing\" altogether. Probably the former one. I suspect that they indeed describe different actions, but for me having the \"Indexing\" with its own progress report would be enough.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "My (initial) concern was that using the same full-height line separator for Progress and Indexing would make it easy to mix them up with the clock.\n\nFair point. Whichever design works for you.\n\nLet me know what you think would suit as a shorter form! I don't personally have a knack for designing in general, so suggestions here are always welcome!\n\nI'd personally remove either \"Progress\" or \"Indexing\" altogether. Probably the former one. I suspect that they indeed describe different actions, but for me having the \"Indexing\" with its own progress report would be enough.",
